-- The STM32H753's memory with its Cortex-M7's level 1 caches on: the
-- regions, placements, stack and float unit of devices/descriptions/
-- stm32h753, the same chip's cacheless profile, and the caches (D974).
-- Written by hand; see devices/README.md for the sources it was checked
-- against.
--
-- The profile is cached: compiler-owned reset invalidates the 16 KiB data
-- cache by set and way and the 16 KiB instruction cache, once .data, .bss
-- and .ramtext are written, and enables both; the entry's return cleans
-- and invalidates the data cache and disables both (D973).  Each has
-- 32-byte lines, and the M7's are the only level: the chip has no level 2
-- cache.  With the MPU off the default memory map applies: the SRAM
-- region, 0x2000_0000 to 0x3FFF_FFFF, which holds the AXI SRAM and SRAM1
-- to SRAM4, is normal, write-back and write-allocate; the code region,
-- flash at 0x0800_0000 among it, is write-through and read-only here;
-- the ITCM and DTCM are tightly coupled and never cached; and the
-- peripherals and the System Control Space are device and strongly
-- ordered memory, never cached.  Data, BSS and the stack are in the AXI
-- SRAM, which the CPU and both DMA controllers reach at 0x2400_0000 and
-- no other address; a buffer placed in another SRAM by name is cached as
-- well, and an alias the chip gives a region is outside this profile.
-- A buffer a DMA stream reads or writes is therefore cached, and is
-- maintained through core/cache's provider in platform/cortex_m/l1:
-- aligned to 32 bytes and a whole number of lines, so that no line it
-- shares holds a byte it does not own, and cleaned before a transmit,
-- cleaned and invalidated before a receive is armed and invalidated once
-- the receive is complete.  A DMA stream
-- observes memory once the maintenance and the completion barrier after
-- it have completed.
--
-- The STM32H753's Cortex-M7 has a float unit, FPv5-D16, which makes the
-- build hard-float at --level=armv7e-m (D615).
--
-- DMA1 and DMA2 cannot reach the DTCM or the ITCM, which only the CPU and
-- the MDMA reach, so initialized data, BSS and the stack, where prototype
-- 1's DMA buffers are, are placed in the AXI SRAM, which both reach. A
-- declaration placed in DTCM with link(region: "DTCM") must not be a
-- buffer a DMA stream reads or writes.

linker.region("FLASH", 0x0800_0000, 2 * 1024 * 1024, "rx")
linker.region("ITCM", 0x0000_0000, 64 * 1024, "rwx")
linker.region("DTCM", 0x2000_0000, 128 * 1024, "rw")
linker.region("AXI_SRAM", 0x2400_0000, 512 * 1024, "rwx")
linker.region("SRAM1", 0x3000_0000, 128 * 1024, "rw")
linker.region("SRAM2", 0x3002_0000, 128 * 1024, "rw")
linker.region("SRAM3", 0x3004_0000, 32 * 1024, "rw")
linker.region("SRAM4", 0x3800_0000, 64 * 1024, "rw")
compiler.boot("vector-table")
compiler.float_unit("fpv5-d16")
compiler.cache("armv7-m-l1", 32)
linker.place("vectors", "FLASH")
linker.place("text", "ITCM")
linker.place("rodata", "FLASH")
linker.place("data", "AXI_SRAM")
linker.place("bss", "AXI_SRAM")
linker.place("stack", "AXI_SRAM", 16 * 1024)
